# Cover every change with a test

Every change ships with a test that exercises it. How depends on the change:

- Fixing a defect or changing existing behaviour: write the test FIRST -
  reproduce the fault, watch it fail, then change the code until it passes.
- Building something new (a module or function that does not exist yet):
  implement it, then leave it covered by tests that pass. Do NOT write tests
  against an interface you have not designed yet.

A change without a test that exercises it is not finished. Never write a stub
test just to satisfy this rule.
